            {
              "id": "CVE-2023-45289-stdlib",
              "name": "GoModuleMatcherCpeMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2023-45289 medium vulnerability for stdlib package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "When following an HTTP redirect to a domain which is not a subdomain match or exact match of the initial domain, an http.Client does not forward sensitive headers such as \"Authorization\" or \"Cookie\". For example, a redirect from foo.com to www.foo.com will forward the Authorization header, but a redirect to bar.com will not. A maliciously crafted HTTP redirect could cause sensitive headers to be unexpectedly forwarded."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/anchore/grype",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2023-45289\nSeverity: medium\nPackage: stdlib\nVersion: go1.21.3\nFix Version: 1.21.8,1.21.8,1.22.1,1.22.1\nType: go-module\nLocation: /bin/workflow-controller\nData Namespace: nvd:cpe\nLink: [CVE-2023-45289](https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2023-45289)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2023-45289**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| medium  | stdlib  | go1.21.3  | 1.21.8,1.21.8,1.22.1,1.22.1  | go-module  | /bin/workflow-controller  | nvd:cpe  | [CVE-2023-45289](https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2023-45289)  |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:golang/stdlib@1.21.3"
                ],
                "security-severity": "4.3"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2023-45290-stdlib",
              "name": "GoModuleMatcherCpeMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2023-45290 medium vulnerability for stdlib package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "When parsing a multipart form (either explicitly with Request.ParseMultipartForm or implicitly with Request.FormValue, Request.PostFormValue, or Request.FormFile), limits on the total size of the parsed form were not applied to the memory consumed while reading a single form line. This permits a maliciously crafted input containing very long lines to cause allocation of arbitrarily large amounts of memory, potentially leading to memory exhaustion. With fix, the ParseMultipartForm function now correctly limits the maximum size of form lines."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/anchore/grype",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2023-45290\nSeverity: medium\nPackage: stdlib\nVersion: go1.21.3\nFix Version: 1.21.8,1.22.1\nType: go-module\nLocation: /bin/workflow-controller\nData Namespace: nvd:cpe\nLink: [CVE-2023-45290](https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2023-45290)",
