              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2025-22873 low vulnerability for stdlib package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "It was possible to improperly access the parent directory of an os.Root by opening a filename ending in \"../\". For example, Root.Open(\"../\") would open the parent directory of the Root. This escape only permits opening the parent directory itself, not ancestors of the parent or files contained within the parent."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/anchore/grype",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2025-22873\nSeverity: low\nPackage: stdlib\nVersion: go1.21.3\nFix Version: 1.23.9,1.24.3\nType: go-module\nLocation: /bin/workflow-controller\nData Namespace: nvd:cpe\nLink: [CVE-2025-22873](https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2025-22873)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2025-22873**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| low  | stdlib  | go1.21.3  | 1.23.9,1.24.3  | go-module  | /bin/workflow-controller  | nvd:cpe  | [CVE-2025-22873](https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2025-22873)  |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:golang/stdlib@1.21.3"
                ],
                "security-severity": "3.8"
              }
